1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,980
The world is programmed to distract you.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,580
The world doesn't want you to fail.

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,220
It wants something even worse.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:06,840
It wants you distracted.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,160
Think about it. Every single day, millions of people wake up,

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,740
grab their phones, and immediately begin scrolling.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,160
They watch videos. They check notifications.

8
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,900
They look at other people's lives.

9
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,140
And before they even realize it, an hour has disappeared.

10
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:23,680
But here's the scary part.

11
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,840
And the next day. And the next.

12
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:32,020
Until one day, they look back and realize they've spent years watching other

13
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,660
people accomplish the things they always dreamed of doing.

14
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:35,840
Imagine two people.

15
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,280
They both wake up at 7am.

16
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,460
They both have the same 24 hours.

17
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,700
They both have dreams of becoming successful.

18
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,120
But they make two completely different decisions.

19
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,080
The first person grabs his phone.

20
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,480
He watches one video.

21
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,720
Then another. Then another.

22
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:55,640
He tells himself he's only going to scroll for five minutes.

23
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,820
Minutes. But five minutes turns into 30.

24
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,380
30 turns into an hour.

25
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,840
And suddenly, half his morning is gone.

26
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,420
The second person wakes up and gets straight to work.

27
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,220
He reads a few pages of a book.

28
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:09,520
He exercises. He learns a new skill.

29
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:14,220
Neither person realizes it yet, but their small decisions are creating two

30
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,540
completely different futures.

31
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,760
I'll learn that skill when things slow down.

32
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:22,100
Another video. You need to stop giving away the time you already have.

33
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:25,460
Because every minute you spend doing nothing is a minute you can never get

34
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,180
back. Imagine looking 10 years into the future.

35
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:29,880
You see two versions of yourself.

36
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,760
One version spent every day chasing entertainment.

37
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,340
He watched other people travel.

38
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,440
He watched other people build businesses.

39
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,920
He constantly told himself that one day he would do the same.

40
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,300
But that day never came.

41
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,140
Now look at the other version.

42
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,780
He wasn't perfect. He still had bad days.

43
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:48,560
He still got tired.

44
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:50,740
Sometimes he wanted to quit.

45
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,480
But he kept showing up.

46
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:56,800
While everyone else was scrolling, He was learning while everyone else was

47
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:00,540
making excuses. He was working while everyone else was waiting for motivation

48
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:04,360
He was building discipline and ten years later the difference between these

49
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:08,860
two people is enormous not because one had more talent Not because one had

50
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:09,540
more opportunities.

51
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,800
So how do you escape the distraction trap?

52
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:17,120
You start small Put your phone away when you wake up stop checking notifications

53
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:21,620
every five minutes set goals that actually matter to you Spend 30 minutes

54
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,560
learning something valuable exercise

55
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:26,200
Read, build something.

56
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:30,580
And most importantly, learn how to be comfortable doing things that aren't

57
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:33,240
entertaining. Because success isn't always exciting.

58
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,980
Sometimes it's sitting alone, working on something nobody cares about yet.

59
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,840
Sometimes it's repeating the same task hundreds of times.

60
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,040
Sometimes it's choosing to keep going when you don't feel motivated.

61
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,040
That's the part most people never see.

62
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:46,640
They see the successful person.

63
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:47,920
They see the money.

64
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:49,960
They see the lifestyle.

65
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,660
But they don't see the thousands of hours spent working when nobody was

66
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,660
watching. Here's something you need to understand.

67
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,020
Your phone isn't necessarily your enemy.

68
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,780
Entertainment isn't your enemy.

69
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,760
Taking a break isn't your enemy.

70
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,900
The problem begins when you lose control.

71
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,760
When you can no longer sit in silence.

72
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,820
When you can't focus for 10 minutes without checking your phone.

73
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:12,580
When you spend more time watching other people chase their dreams than actually

74
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,840
chasing your own. That's when you need to make a change.

75
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,380
Because your attention is one of the most valuable things you own.

76
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,140
And where you spend your attention is where you spend your life.

77
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:22,960
So the next time you pick up your phone,

78
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,420
ask yourself one question.

79
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:25,840
Am I using this device?

80
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,920
Or is this device using me?

81
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,580
You only get one life.

82
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:32,520
Don't spend it watching everybody else live theirs.

83
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,720
Put the phone down.

84
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:37,660
Stop waiting. Stop making excuses.

85
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,280
And start building.

86
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:43,740
Because five years from now, you'll either be proud of the decisions you're

87
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,740
making today, or you'll wish you had made them.

88
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,340
The choice is yours.
